# Build output: everything here is regenerated by `make all`.
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Sweep evidence.  The JSONL files are large (5-6 MB each) and take hours to
# produce, so they are kept locally in results/ and regenerated on demand with
# `make oracle-leds-full` / `make oracle-dense-addrem`.  The acceptance reports
# and run logs next to them ARE tracked, because those are what the findings
# document cites.
results/*.jsonl
results/*.jsonl.tmp

# ...but the gzipped archives ARE tracked: they compress ~40x (a 5.7 MB sweep
# becomes 141 KB), so the evidence travels with the repository instead of
# existing only on one machine.  `make archive` regenerates them.

# Stale byproducts that predate the Makefile flow; `make all` regenerates the
# real ones under build/.
work/dense.json
work/*_pnr.log
work/*_yosys.log
work/leds_mut.asc
work/leds_mut.bin
work/leds_mut.v
work/leds_rt_sim.v
work/leds_mut2_sim.v
results/*.log

# The completed sweeps are archived as results/archive/*.jsonl.gz instead.
